//
// A WRITE through the enum to a field its variants lay out at different offsets has no one
// place to land, so it is refused, naming the cure: declare the field first in every variant
// (loft#2441).  Before, `e.n = 5` on a `KIce` wrote `KIce.m`, silently, on both backends.
//
// @falsified-at: d813c6115 — interpret: compiled with no diagnostic -> the refusal (the write
//   landed in `KIce.m`); measured by hand against the build without the refusal.
//   CHANNEL: expect-error — the refusal's text.
//   WITNESS: no diagnostic there (the program ran, writing `KIce.m`); the refusal here.
//   HOLDS: nothing else in the file is measured.
// @FR-C-Var.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: this field sits at a different offset in each variant that declares it

enum KEnt { KFire { n: integer, s: text }, KIce { m: integer, n: integer } }

fn put(e: KEnt) { e.n = 5; }

fn main() {
  b = KIce { m: 1, n: 7 };
  put(b);
}
